# Phase 2: Zephyr Integration & Embedded Deployment

## Preconditions
```
@pre: COOS native (Phase 1) verified and stable
@pre: API surface frozen and WIT-complete
```

## Invariants
```
□inv: RAM constraint {StrictMemoryLimit} 64KB maintained
□inv: No dynamic memory allocation {Policy_Memory} — static/stack only
□inv: C++20 coroutines {UseCpp20Coroutine} remain core scheduling mechanism
□inv: No RTTI, no exceptions {embedded_cpp_rule} enforced
□inv: Zephyr RTOS independent from COOS kernel (COOS is a module, not replacement)
```

## Goals
```
◇goal: Cortex-M33 and RISC-V targets boot and run COOS natively
◇goal: Zephyr board definitions (DTS, Kconfig) manage cross-compilation via west
◇goal: west build -b <board> && west flash && west debug workflow functional
```

## Postconditions
```
@post: COOS API unchanged from Phase 1
@post: HAL drivers integrated via IPC Router
@post: vSoC runtime functional on embedded targets
```

## Design Notes

- **COOS remains single-threaded, cooperative** — No preemption by Zephyr kernel scheduler
- **Zephyr provides HAL/BSP only** — COOS is independent kernel module
- **embedded_cpp_rule applies strictly** — See `.agents/rules/embedded_cpp_rule.md`
- **Cross-compilation via Zephyr SDK** — arm-zephyr-eabi, riscv64-zephyr-elf toolchains
- **Memory budget: 64KB total** — Includes COOS, IPC, vSoC, application
